# Client rules for authentication and token exchange (YAML-LD, format 0.12.0).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: Authentication and token exchange, as a client does them
comment: >-
  What a client's requests to the session's token endpoint must satisfy: the token exchange of
  lws10-core section 5.2.3, the self-issued credentials of the CID suite, and the token types of
  the OpenID suite's ID Tokens and the SAML suite's assertions. The session's identities, alice and
  bob, have identity documents that name a key each, which the developer downloads from the session
  page, and the session's own OpenID Provider; the session's SAML identity provider hands out
  assertions about them through the session API. The session's authorization server trusts those
  and nothing else.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-openid-20260803/
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-saml-20260803/
entries:

  # ---- every token request ----

  - id: "#client-token-exchange-resource"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-token-exchange-resource
    label: The client's token exchange requests name the storage they want a token for in resource
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authorization-token-exchange-request
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authz]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-resource-param
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      form:
        - pointer: /grant_type
          equals: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
    expect:
      form:
        - pointer: /resource
          jsonType: string
          matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Send resource with every token exchange request: the realm of the storage's 401 challenge,
      an absolute URI. The access token's aud is made from it.

  - id: "#client-token-exchange-subject-token"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-token-exchange-subject-token
    label: The client's token exchange requests present an authentication credential in subject_token
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authorization-token-exchange-request
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authz]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-subject-token-param
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      form:
        - pointer: /grant_type
          equals: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
    expect:
      form:
        - pointer: /subject_token
          jsonType: string
          matches: "."
    guidance: >-
      Send the authentication credential, a self-issued JWT, an ID Token or a SAML assertion, as
      subject_token, with its type in subject_token_type. Not as assertion, id_token or another
      parameter.

  - id: "#client-token-for-containing-realm"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-token-for-containing-realm
    label: After a 401, the client asks for a token only for a realm that contains the URL it was refused
    comment: >-
      A client must check that the URL it requested is within the realm of the challenge before
      it acts on it. The session's root container lists a decoy whose 401 names a realm that does
      not contain it, so a client that does not check asks the authorization server for a token
      for that realm. Each 401 from the storage opens a trigger, and the client's next token
      request is the trial. The task arms tokenExpired, so that a client which keeps its token
      has a reason to ask for a new one after meeting the decoy.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authorization-server-discovery
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authz]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-challenge-realm-param
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Open the first entry of the storage's root container, then any resource you can read. The
        session answers that request once with 401, as if your access token had expired: get a
        new token and try again.
      arm: tokenExpired
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      form:
        - pointer: /resource
          jsonType: string
      after:
        server: storage
        statusCode: 401
    expect:
      realmContainsRequest: true
    guidance: >-
      Before you ask for a token, check that the URL the 401 answered is within the challenge's
      realm: the realm itself, or below it. If it is not, do not ask for a token for that realm
      or send one to that URL.

  # ---- self-issued credentials (the CID suite) ----

  - id: "#client-cid-token-type-jwt"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-token-type-jwt
    label: The client presents a self-issued credential with the jwt token type
    comment: >-
      A self-issued credential is one the client signed itself, whose kid, iss, sub or client_id
      names one of the session's identities (OBSERVATION.md section 4.9).
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#token-type
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/token-type-jwt
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      form:
        - pointer: /subject_token_type
          equals: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
    guidance: >-
      Send subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt with a JWT you signed yourself.

  - id: "#client-cid-credential-signed"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-credential-signed
    label: The client's self-issued credential is signed, not alg none
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authentication-data-model
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/alg-not-none
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-credential-signed
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        header:
          - pointer: /alg
            jsonType: string
            matches: "(?i)^(?!none$)."
    guidance: >-
      Sign the JWT with the identity's key, ES256 for the session's P-256 keys, and name the key's
      verification method in kid. An unsigned JWT (alg none) is never a credential.

  - id: "#client-cid-subject-claim"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-subject-claim
    label: The client's self-issued credential names its subject, a URI, in sub
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authentication-data-model
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/sub-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-subject-claim-uri
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-credential-tamper-evident-claims
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /sub
            jsonType: string
            matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Put the identity's URI, the URL of its identity document, in sub.

  - id: "#client-cid-issuer-claim"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-issuer-claim
    label: The client's self-issued credential names its issuer, a URI, in iss
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authentication-data-model
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/iss-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-issuer-claim-uri
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /iss
            jsonType: string
            matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Put the issuer in iss. For a self-issued credential that is the subject's own URI.

  - id: "#client-cid-client-id-claim"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-client-id-claim
    label: The client's self-issued credential names the client in client_id
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authentication-data-model
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/client-id-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-client-claim
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /client_id
            jsonType: string
    guidance: >-
      Put the client identifier in client_id. For a self-issued credential that is the subject's
      own URI.

  - id: "#client-cid-identifiers-agree"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-identifiers-agree
    label: The client's self-issued credential has the same URI in sub, iss and client_id
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/sub-iss-client-same-uri
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /sub
            jsonType: string
          - pointer: /iss
            jsonType: string
          - pointer: /client_id
            jsonType: string
    expect:
      identifiersAgree: true
    guidance: >-
      Use the identity's URI for all three of sub, iss and client_id: a self-issued credential is
      an agent speaking for itself.

  - id: "#client-cid-audience-includes-as"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-audience-includes-as
    label: The audience of the client's self-issued credential includes the authorization server
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/aud-includes-as
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /aud
            exists: true
    expect:
      audienceIncludesAs: true
    guidance: >-
      Put the authorization server's issuer identifier, the as_uri of the storage's challenge, in
      aud, alone or in an array.

  - id: "#client-cid-audience-restricted"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-audience-restricted
    label: The client's self-issued credential restricts its audience with aud
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#authentication-data-model
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authn-audience-restriction-recommended
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /aud
            exists: true
    guidance: >-
      Restrict the credential to the authorization server you present it to, with an aud claim,
      so that nobody who sees it can use it elsewhere.

  - id: "#client-cid-expiry-claim"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-expiry-claim
    label: The client's self-issued credential says when it expires, in exp
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/exp-claim
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /exp
            jsonType: number
    guidance: >-
      Put the expiry time in exp, in seconds since the epoch: a few minutes from now is plenty.

  - id: "#client-cid-issued-at-claim"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-cid-issued-at-claim
    label: The client's self-issued credential says when it was issued, in iat
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/#serialization
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-ssi-cid/iat-claim
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: selfIssued
    expect:
      credential:
        claims:
          - pointer: /iat
            jsonType: number
    guidance: >-
      Put the time you signed the credential in iat, in seconds since the epoch.

  # ---- ID Tokens (the OpenID suite) ----

  - id: "#client-oidc-token-type-id-token"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-oidc-token-type-id-token
    label: The client presents an ID Token with the id_token token type
    comment: >-
      The trials are token requests presenting an ID Token the session's OpenID Provider issued.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-openid-20260803/#token-type
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-openid/id-token-token-type-uri
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: openidProvider
    expect:
      form:
        - pointer: /subject_token_type
          equals: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:id_token
    guidance: >-
      Send subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:id_token with an ID Token. Not jwt,
      which is for credentials the client signs itself.

  # ---- SAML 2.0 assertions (format 0.12.0) ----

  - id: "#client-saml-token-type-saml2"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-saml-token-type-saml2
    label: The client presents a SAML 2.0 assertion with the saml2 token type
    comment: >-
      The trials are token requests presenting an assertion the session's SAML identity provider
      issued: base64url-encoded, as RFC 8693 section 3 defines the saml2 token type, or in another
      base64 form of the same assertion. The assertion's own content binds the identity provider,
      not the client, so no rule judges it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-saml-20260803/#token-type
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    area: authentication
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-authn-saml/token-type-saml2
    observe:
      role: asToken
      method: POST
      credentialSource: samlIdentityProvider
    expect:
      form:
        - pointer: /subject_token_type
          equals: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:saml2
    guidance: >-
      Send subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:saml2 with a SAML assertion, which
      goes base64url-encoded in subject_token. Not jwt or id_token, which are for JWTs.
